AUTOMATING LOGIN PAGE IN PLAYWRIGHT USING JAVASCRIPT
--------------------------------

Playwright can automate the login process by locating the username
and password fields, entering the required credentials, and clicking
the Login button.

Example:

import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('Login Page Test', async ({ page }) => {

    await page.goto('https://rahulshettyacademy.com/loginpagePractise/');

    await page.locator('#username').fill('rahulshettyacademy');

    await page.locator('#password').fill('Learning@830$3mK2');

    await page.locator('#signInBtn').click();

});


Execution Flow:

import Playwright
      ↓
Define test
      ↓
Open Login Page
      ↓
Enter Username
      ↓
Enter Password
      ↓
Click Login


Explanation:

1. Username

await page.locator('#username').fill('rahulshettyacademy');

→ Locates the element using its ID `username`
→ Enters the username using `fill()`


2. Password

await page.locator('#password').fill('Learning@830$3mK2');

→ Locates the password field using its ID `password`
→ Enters the password using `fill()`


3. Login Button

await page.locator('#signInBtn').click();

→ Locates the Login button using its ID `signInBtn`
→ Clicks the button to submit the login form


Important:

`await` is used because these Playwright actions are asynchronous.
Playwright waits for each action to complete before moving to the
next statement.

Here:

test → Defines the test case
page → Playwright page fixture
page.goto() → Opens the URL
locator() → Identifies the element
fill() → Enters text
click() → Clicks the button
await → Waits for each operation to complete

