--------------------------------
PRINTING AND VERIFYING ERROR MESSAGE
--------------------------------

1. Print the Error Message

console.log(await page.locator("[style*='block']").textContent());

→ Locates the error message.
→ Gets the text using textContent().
→ Prints the actual error message in the console.


2. Verify the Error Message

await expect(page.locator("[style*='block']"))
    .toContainText('Incorrect');

→ Locates the error message.
→ Verifies that the message contains the text "Incorrect".
→ If "Incorrect" is present → Test PASSES.
→ If "Incorrect" is not present → Test FAILS.


Key Difference:

console.log()
    ↓
Prints the actual text.

expect().toContainText()
    ↓
Verifies the expected text.


Easy Way to Remember:

PRINT → console.log()

VERIFY → expect()

--------------------------------
textContent() vs toContainText()
--------------------------------

textContent()
→ Gets the actual text from the located element.

Example:
await page.locator("[style*='block']").textContent();


toContainText('Incorrect')
→ Verifies that the located element contains the expected text "Incorrect".

Example:
await expect(page.locator("[style*='block']"))
    .toContainText('Incorrect');


Easy Way to Remember:

textContent()
    ↓
GET the text

toContainText()
    ↓
VERIFY the text

